{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Type Filtering.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Type Filtering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linq type filtering linq type filtering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Type Filtering.md","fileName":"LINQ Type Filtering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"LINQ Type Filtering","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[LINQ Query Construction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["LINQ Query Construction","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Type Filtering.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Type Filtering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linq type filtering linq type filtering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Type Filtering.md","fileName":"LINQ Type Filtering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"LINQ Type Filtering","heading":"LINQ Type Filtering","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"`OfType<T>` filters a heterogeneous sequence to elements compatible with a requested type and returns them as that type. Incompatible values, including null values when the target requires an object of the chosen type, are omitted rather than causing a cast failure.\n\nThis differs from `Cast<T>`, which attempts to cast every element and fails when an item is incompatible. Type filtering is therefore useful when a mixed sequence is expected and only one subtype is relevant to the next stage of a query.","tags":["baby"],"links":["LINQ Query Construction","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Type Filtering.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/LINQ Type Filtering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchNa